1.52.m:
“I continually do what is commanded by Rāma; I worship Rāma with reverence;
all sin has been removed by Rāma; salutation to you, O Rāma!
Liberation is always desired by me from Rāma; I am a servant of Rāma;
may my mind take delight purely in Rāma; O Rāma, salutation to you!”

acorayat, corayet, coryāt, acūcurat, acoriṣyat—such indeed are the ten verb classes;
in the causative: bhāvayati; with the affix san in expressing desire: bubhūṣati;
in intensive repetition of an action, the learned use bobhūyate, O sage;

likewise, with elision of yaṅ [yaṅluk], bobhavīti is taught;
putrīyati in the sense of desiring for oneself, and also in behaving like [a son], O Nārada;
